--- Calls a function with an array of arguments.
---
--- @details
--- `apply` takes a pair `[f, args]` and invokes `f` with `args` as its
--- argument list. It is the arrow-level counterpart of a spread call:
--- useful when the argument list is computed or stored in a variable
--- rather than written literally at the call site.
---
--- @example
--- `[[x, y]~> x + y, [1, 2]] >>> comb.apply`
--- -- => 3
---
export apply :: [f, args]~> (args >>> f)
